In the ever-growing search for the perfect enclosure to help expand your local mesh, you see a lot of options out there. Do you 3D print a custom enclosure? Head to the home improvement store and buy out half the plumbing and electrical aisle? Or maybe you repurpose something that was never designed to hold a node in the first place?

For this build, we are going to go with option three.

In my own quest to build a more robust tree node, I stumbled across a few mentions of using a solar buoy and decided to investigate myself. 

